-- title:
--   Kummer covers are unramified at places where u is a unit
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and let $F$, $F'$ be fields equipped with $k$-algebra structures. Let $\varphi \colon F \to F'$ be a $k$-algebra homomorphism whose underlying ring homomorphism is integral, so every element of $F'$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\varphi(F)$. Let $n$ be a natural number whose image in $k$ is nonzero, and let $c \in F'$ be such that the subfield of $F'$ generated by $\varphi(F) \cup \{c\}$ is all of $F'$. Assume $u \in F$ satisfies $\varphi(u) = c^{\,n}$. Let $P$ be a place of $F'$ over $k$, that is, a valuation subring of $F'$ containing the image of $k$, different from $F'$ itself and a principal ideal ring. Write $v =$ `P.restrictAlong φ hφ` for the place of $F$ whose valuation subring is the preimage of that of $P$ under $\varphi$. Assume $v$ is rational, i.e. the map from $k$ to the residue field of $v$ is surjective, and that both $u$ and $u^{-1}$ lie in the valuation subring of $v$. Then the ramification index of $P$ along $\varphi$, namely the least positive integer of the form $\operatorname{ord}_P(\varphi f)$ with $f \in F$, $f \neq 0$, equals $1$.
--
--   This is the unramified case of the standard ramification formula for Kummer extensions $c^{\,n} = u$ with $n$ invertible in the constant field, where $e = n/\gcd(n, v(u))$: at a rational place of $F$ at which $u$ is a unit the covering is unramified. It feeds the genus comparison [`AlgebraicCurve.genusFF_eq_of_finrankAlong_eq_of_pow_eq_X_sub_X_pow`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.genusFF_eq_of_finrankAlong_eq_of_pow_eq_X_sub_X_pow) and the place census and genus computation for the Drinfeld curve.
